{"ts":"2026-08-26T19:15:29.547Z","author":"claude","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"f559dcd5a5f387bc7221097a","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"Likely shape: an --entry-from <field> flag accepting close_reason first, since a closed issue already states its resolution there and the pm CLI records it as part of the close transition. Items without the field fall back to title so no existing repo changes behaviour."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pmc-d3ds"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"A defect-shaped item title renders backwards under a Fixed heading, and there is no second field to draw the entry from"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"pm-changelog projects the item title directly into the changelog entry. Issue trackers want a defect-shaped title that names what is wrong, and Keep a Changelog wants an entry under Fixed that describes the change. Those two conventions produce opposite sentences from the same string, so a repo must pick one and be wrong in the other place. This surfaced in review twice in one session with contradictory guidance: pm-linear was told to make a title defect-shaped, and pm-changelog was told the resulting entry describes the defect rather than the fix. Both reviews were right about their own surface. The generator has no field other than title to draw from, so neither convention can be satisfied without breaking the other."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Feature"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["changelog","dx"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-26T19:15:29.547Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-26T19:15:29.547Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/deadline","value":"2026-09-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/assignee","value":"claude"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"claude"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":240},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The generator can source an entry from a field other than title, with an explicit opt-in flag and a documented fallback to title when the field is absent; the choice is recorded so changelog check and generation agree; a test proves an item with a defect-shaped title and a fix-shaped alternate field renders the alternate under Fixed"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pmc-n07l","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-26T19:15:29.547Z","author":"claude","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-26T19:15:29.547Z","author":"claude","text":"Worked around in the immediate case by retitling pmc-n07l to a change-shaped sentence, which matches this repo's existing entries. That workaround costs the tracker its defect-shaped title."}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-26T19:15:29.547Z","author":"claude","text":"Both review findings that motivated this are legitimate on their own surface; the conflict is in the generator, not in either reviewer."}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/learnings","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-26T19:15:29.547Z","author":"claude","text":"When two conventions disagree about the same string, the defect is usually the single string, not either convention."}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/files","value":[{"path":"src/generator.ts","scope":"project"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tests","value":[{"command":"npm test","scope":"project"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/docs","value":[{"path":"https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/","scope":"project","note":"the changelog convention the entry side must satisfy"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"bb6f114e8a17229cff578ff1b1431829f53887723ca607986e4a7ee3ea3bc09c","item_hash_version":2,"message":"Track the title-versus-entry conflict the review round exposed","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
